{"code":"BIO 100A","title":"Exb: Secret Life of Plants","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"A thematic course exploring five fundamental features of all biological systems, including structure and function, information flow, energy and matter, interactions, and evolution. Most ecosystems on Earth are shaped by plant life. While it may not seem like it, plants constantly do the same things we do: search for nutrients, secrete hormones, and defend themselves. In this course, we will explore the incredible adaptations plants use to survive and grow, compare these to adaptations of animals, and examine how plants provide the foundation for both ecosystems and human society. Students must concurrently enroll in a BIO 100L lab section. Not open to students who have taken any other Explorations in Biology course.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/100/bio-100a","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"G027","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R","Soc, Struct & Inst Hier"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":30,"comments":"Open to Srs., Jrs., Soph., & 1st Yr Not open to those who took BIO 100*. Must also sign up for a BIO-100L section.","end_time":"09:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"G027","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"09:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"09:00"},{"days":"R","room":"G027","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"17:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Pete Guiden"]}]},
{"code":"BIO 100D","title":"Exb: Diagnostic Odyssey","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"A thematic course exploring five fundamental features of all biological systems, including structure and function, information flow, energy and matter, interactions, and evolution. For people-usually, young children-with symptoms of a rare genetic condition, pinpointing the molecular and genetic cause often requires an arduous \"diagnostic odyssey.\" But a correct diagnosis can be life-changing. This course will explore universal biological principles through the lens of rare human genetic disorders. We will survey the myriad ways that DNA mutates, how these mutations instigate changes in cells and organs, how the variant genes are inherited, and how this knowledge can inform genetic counseling and treatment plans. Students must concurrently enroll in a BIO 100L lab section. Not open to students who have taken any other Explorations in Biology course.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/100/bio-100d","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"G027","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R","Soc, Struct & Inst Hier"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":30,"comments":null,"end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"G027","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"10:00"},{"days":"W","room":"G027","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"22:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"19:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Ivan Bochkov"]}]},
{"code":"BIO 100E","title":"Exb: Microbes Rule!","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"A thematic course exploring five fundamental features of all biological systems, including structure and function, information flow, energy and matter, interactions, and evolution. From early in Earth's history to the present, microbes have ruled our planet. Recent advances in DNA sequencing reveal a vast, complex and diverse microbial world living around and within us (our personal microbiomes). This course examines the origin, function, and diversity of microbial life on our planet and explores recent discoveries in host-microbiome research. Students must concurrently enroll in a BIO 100L lab section. Not open to students who have taken any other Explorations in Biology course.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/100/bio-100e","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"203","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R","Soc, Struct & Inst Hier"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","capacity":30,"comments":"Open to Srs., Jrs., Soph., & 1st Yr Not open to those who took BIO 100*. Must also sign up for a BIO-100L section.","end_time":"09:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"203","type":"LEC","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"09:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"09:00"},{"days":"R","room":"203","type":"FINAL","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"17:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Michael L. McCormick"]}]},
{"code":"BIO 100I","title":"Exb: You Are What You Eat","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"A thematic course exploring five fundamental features of all biological systems, including structure and function, information flow, energy and matter, interactions, and evolution. Acquisition of food resources and adaptations to maximize their utilization are key drivers of the diversity of life. We will explore resource acquisition from cellular, ecological, and evolutionary perspectives. We will also cover important aspects of how our own changing diet has driven human evolution, anatomy, and health outcomes. All living beings truly are a reflection of what they eat! Students must concurrently enroll in a BIO 100L lab section. Not open to students who have taken any other Explorations in Biology course.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/100/bio-100i","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"127","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R","Soc, Struct & Inst Hier"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","capacity":30,"comments":null,"end_time":"09:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"127","type":"LEC","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"09:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"09:00"},{"days":"R","room":"127","type":"FINAL","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"17:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Jason M. Townsend"]}]},
