{"code":"BIO 214","title":"Health Care Systems","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"An overview and analysis of US health care systems. US health care systems include public health (population-based services) and medical care (individual patients) systems. Topics include development and organization of various public health and medical entities within the United States, strengths and challenges related to cost, quality, and access to these systems, past and present epidemics, and current issues related to health care systems. May not be counted toward the concentration or minor. Not open to students who have taken Bio 216. Next offered TBD.","cross_listed":["PPOL 214","SOC 214"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/200/bio-214","sections":[{"days":"W","room":"211","types":["Co-Lab Course","Proseminar"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Burke Library","capacity":16,"comments":"Open to Fall 2026 Justice Lab students only.","end_time":"16:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"W","room":"211","type":"LEC","building":"Burke Library","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"},{"days":"R","room":"211","type":"FINAL","building":"Burke Library","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"12:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Herman K. Lehman"]}]},
{"code":"BIO 222","title":"Human Anatomy","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"Exploration of the structure and function of human tissues, organs and systems with an introduction to basic pathology and diagnostic tools. This course emphasizes physiological function and the role of anatomical form in these processes. Examines skeletal, muscular, endocrine, cardiovascular, gastrointestinal, and reproductive systems of humans. Thoughtful dissections of animal model systems and analysis of histology will be the focus of the laboratory. Prerequisites, 100, or 101, or 102, or 115, or consent of instructor. Three hours of class and three hours of laboratory.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/200/bio-222","sections":[{"days":"TR","room":"210","types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Root Hall","capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"11:45:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"210","type":"LEC","building":"Root Hall","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"11:45","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"10:30"},{"days":"T","room":"210","type":"FINAL","building":"Root Hall","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"17:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"10:30:00","instructors":["Beth A. Eischen"]}]},
