{"code":"BIO 354","title":"Bio Mech Neuropsych Disease","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"Neuropsychiatric diseases (such as schizophrenia, autism spectrum disorder, and Alzheimer's) frequently produce recognizable symptoms; however, their molecular origins remain a mystery. In this course, we will investigate what is known about these diseases and examine unanswered questions about their underlying mechanisms. We will delve into the recent primary literature, learn about current research techniques, and explore cutting-edge treatment options.","cross_listed":["NEURO 354"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/300/bio-354","sections":[{"days":"MW","room":"3021","types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"14:15:00","meetings":[{"days":"MW","room":"3021","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"14:15","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"},{"days":"R","room":"3021","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"12:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Abigail K. Myers"]}]},
{"code":"BIO 419W","title":"Life & the Seasons","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"How do organisms adapt to seasonal changes in their environment? Almost all habitats have multiple seasons, characterized by somewhat predictable changes in temperature, light, or precipitation. Organisms have many adaptations to such seasonal dynamics (\"phenology\"). In this course, we will identify common phenological adaptations, and explore the value of these adaptations in habitats strongly influenced by climate change and invasive species. We will also track phenology of organisms on campus and analyze the forces driving these patterns. Prerequisites, BIO-100.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/400/bio-419","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"2048","types":["Writing Intensive Courses"],"status":"waitlisted","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":18,"comments":"Open to Seniors and Juniors","end_time":"11:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"2048","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"11:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"11:00"},{"days":"T","room":"2048","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"22:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"19:00"}],"start_time":"11:00:00","instructors":["Pete Guiden"]}]},
{"code":"BIO 431","title":"Seminar in Immunotherapy","department":"Biology","credits":1,"description":"This seminar examines the principles and applications of immunotherapy across a range of health conditions, including cancer, autoimmunity, and infectious disease. Through close reading and discussion of primary research and reviews, we will explore how immune responses can be activated, redirected, suppressed, or reprogrammed for therapeutic benefit. Topics may include immune tolerance, checkpoint regulation, vaccines, cellular and antibody therapies, and strategies for modulating tissue-specific immunity. Emphasis is placed on close, critical reading of experimental literature and on evaluating current approaches and their limitations in the field through class discussion, written and oral critiques, and an individual final project focused on a current question in immunotherapy research.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/bio-biology/400/bio-431","sections":[{"days":"MW","room":"2072","types":[],"status":"waitlisted","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":12,"comments":null,"end_time":"14:15:00","meetings":[{"days":"MW","room":"2072","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"14:15","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"},{"days":"R","room":"2072","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"12:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Elena Tonc"]}]},
