{"code":"CPSCI 102","title":"Design Principles","department":"Computer Science","credits":1,"description":"A second course in programming, concentrating on principled software design techniques. Topics include class design, effective functional decomposition, recursion, and structured data. Students will continue to develop programming proficiency by writing programs in the C++ programming language. Course discussion will emphasize, efficient implementations in terms of memory space and running time, computational complexity of algorithms, and an introduction to data structures. Three hours of lecture and two hours of laboratory.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/cpsci-computer-science/100/cpsci-102","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"3040","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":40,"comments":"Open to Srs., Jrs., Soph., & 1st Yr","end_time":"09:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"3040","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"09:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"09:00"},{"days":"R","room":"3040","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"17:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Karyn Doke"]}]},
