{"code":"ECON 166","title":"Econ Theory & Evidence","department":"Economics","credits":1,"description":"An introduction to how economists develop and test theory, with a special emphasis on theory explaining the causes and consequences of inequality. The basic concepts of probability and statistics are taught in addition to theories of the labor market, inflation/unemployment tradeoffs, impact of fiscal and monetary policy, externalities, public goods, and international trade. Not open to seniors or students who have taken Math 152 or Math 252 or Math 253 or Math 254 or Math 352. Students who have taken Govt 230 may not register for Econ 166 without permission of the instructor.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/econ-economics/100/econ-166","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"224","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","capacity":40,"comments":"Open to 1st Years, Sophomores & Juniors Only Exclude Math 253 & 352 & 152/252","end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"224","type":"LEC","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"10:00"},{"days":"T","room":"101","type":"FINAL","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"12:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Paul A. Hagstrom"]},{"days":"MWF","room":"224","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"02","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","capacity":40,"comments":"Open to 1st Years, Sophomores & Juniors Only Exclude Math 253 & 352 & 152/252","end_time":"11:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"224","type":"LEC","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"11:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"11:00"},{"days":"T","room":"102","type":"FINAL","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"12:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"11:00:00","instructors":["Paul A. Hagstrom"]}]},
{"code":"ECON 266","title":"Intro to Econometrics","department":"Economics","credits":1,"description":"An introduction to econometric methods that are frequently used in applied economic research. Emphasis on interpreting and critically evaluating empirical results and on establishing the statistical foundations of widely used econometric methods. Topics include the classical linear regression model, functional form, dummy explanatory variables, binary choice models, panel data models, instrumental variables and time series models. Three hours of class and 75 minutes of laboratory. Not open to seniors or students who have taken Econ 400.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/econ-economics/200/econ-266","sections":[{"days":"TR","room":"202","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","capacity":20,"comments":"Open to 1st Years, Sophomores & Juniors Only. Not Open to Those Who Took ECON 400.","end_time":"10:15:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"202","type":"LEC","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"10:15","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"09:00"},{"days":"T","room":"203","type":"LAB","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"14:15","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"},{"days":"R","room":"202","type":"FINAL","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"22:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"19:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Hannah Ruebeck"]},{"days":"TR","room":"202","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"waitlisted","section":"02","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","capacity":20,"comments":"Open to 1st Years, Sophomores & Juniors Only. Not Open to Those Who Took ECON 400.","end_time":"10:15:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"202","type":"LEC","building":"Kirner-Johnson Building","end_date":"