{"code":"MATH 152","title":"Stat Analysis of Data","department":"Mathematics","credits":1,"description":"An introduction to the principles and methods of applied statistics. Topics include exploratory data analysis, sampling distributions, confidence intervals, hypothesis testing, regression analysis, analysis of variance and categorical data analysis. Extensive reliance on statistical computer software and authentic data. May not be taken by students who have taken or are taking Econ 166, Econ 265, Psych 201, Neuro 201 or Govt 230.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/math-mathematics-and-statistics/100/math-152","sections":[{"days":"TR","room":"225","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"C.A. Johnson Bldg.","capacity":40,"comments":"Open to Seniors, Juniors, Sophomores, & 1st Years Exclude Econ 166, 265 & Math 252","end_time":"10:15:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"225","type":"LEC","building":"C.A. Johnson Bldg.","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"10:15","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"09:00"},{"days":"R","room":"225","type":"FINAL","building":"C.A. Johnson Bldg.","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"22:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"19:00"}],"start_time":"09:00:00","instructors":["Chinthaka N. Kuruwita"]}]},
{"code":"MATH 216","title":"Multivariable Calculus","department":"Mathematics","credits":1,"description":"Introduction to functions of more than one variable, partial derivatives, multiple integrals in two and three dimensions, line and surface integrals, Green's Theorem, curl, divergence, the Divergence Theorem and Stokes' Theorem. Prerequisite 116 or placement by the department. Not open to students who have taken 114. The Department. Completion of 216 with a grade of C- or greater carries credit for both 116 and 216 for those students placed into 216.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/math-mathematics-and-statistics/200/math-216","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"222","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"C.A. Johnson Bldg.","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"11:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"222","type":"LEC","building":"C.A. Johnson Bldg.","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"11:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"11:00"},{"days":"T","room":"222","type":"LEC","building":"C.A. Johnson Bldg.","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"12:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"12:00"},{"days":"W","room":"G042","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"12:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"11:00:00","instructors":["Michelle C. LeMasurier"]},{"days":"MWF","room":"201","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"02","building":"Benedict Hall","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"09:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"201","type":"LEC","building":"Benedict Hall","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"09:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"09:00"},{"days":"T","room":"201","type":"LEC","building":"Benedict Hall","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"12:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"12:00"},{"days":"W","room":"207