{"code":"NEURO 331","title":"Physiology","department":"Neuroscience","credits":1,"description":"In this course we will explore the basic principles of physiology and homeostasis focusing on mammalian/human systems and will occasionally explore physiological adaptations in other vertebrate systems. This course will provide a solid foundation in critical thinking, research methods, and data analysis while covering physiological systems including osmoregulation, respiration, digestion, circulation, nerve and muscle function, hormones, immune function, and reproduction.","cross_listed":["BIO 331"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/neuro-neuroscience/300/neuro-331","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"2048","types":["Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"2048","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"10:00"},{"days":"W","room":"2048","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"22:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"19:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Ariel F. Kahrl"]}]},
{"code":"NEURO 331L","title":"Physiology Lab","department":"Neuroscience","credits":0,"description":"This is the lab that is required for the BIO/NEURO 331 lecture series. Both a lab section as well as a lecture section must be taken in the same semester.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/neuro-neuroscience/300/neuro-331","sections":[{"days":"T","room":"2057","types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"16:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"T","room":"2057","type":"LAB","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Ariel F. Kahrl"]},{"days":"W","room":"2057","types":[],"status":"open","section":"02","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"16:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"W","room":"2057","type":"LAB","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Christina E. Schubert"]}]},
{"code":"NEURO 334","title":"Developmental Genetics","department":"Neuroscience","credits":1,"description":"In this course we will integrate classical genetics, epigenetics, cell and molecular biology, and organismal approaches to the study of development. We will analyze a diversity of mechanisms, ranging from ones that set up pattern formation in the unfertilized egg to those governing morphogenesis of organ systems. Topics covered include embryogenesis, gene regulation, axis specification, morphogen signaling, stem cells, cloning, limb formation, and sex determination, as well as congenital defects and issues in human development. Three hours of class and three hours of laboratory.","cross_listed":["BIO 334"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/neuro-neuroscience/300/neuro-334","sections":[{"days":"TR","room":"3024","types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"11:45:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"3024","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"11:45","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"10:30"},{"days":"T","room":"3024","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"17:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"10:30:00","instructors":["Rhea R. Datta"]}]},
{"code":"NEURO 334L","title":"Developmental Genetics Lab","department":"Neuroscience","credits":0,"description":"This is the lab that is required for the BIO/NEURO 334 lecture series. Both a lab section as well as a lecture section must be taken in the same semester.","cross_listed":["BIO 334L"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/neuro-neuroscience/300/neuro-334","sections":[{"days":"W","room":"2058","types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"16:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"W","room":"2058","type":"LAB","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Rhea R. Datta"]},{"days":"R","room":"2058","types":[],"status":"waitlisted","section":"02","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":20,"comments":null,"end_time":"16:00:00","meetings":[{"days":"R","room":"2058","type":"LAB","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"16:00","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Kyle S. Martin"]}]},
{"code":"NEURO 354","title":"Bio Mech Neuropsych Disease","department":"Neuroscience","credits":1,"description":"Neuropsychiatric diseases (such as schizophrenia, autism spectrum disorder, and Alzheimer's) frequently produce recognizable symptoms; however, their molecular origins remain a mystery. In this course, we will investigate what is known about these diseases and examine unanswered questions about their underlying mechanisms. We will delve into the recent primary literature, learn about current research techniques, and explore cutting-edge treatment options.","cross_listed":["BIO 354"],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/neuro-neuroscience/300/neuro-354","sections":[{"days":"MW","room":"3021","types":[],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":40,"comments":null,"end_time":"14:15:00","meetings":[{"days":"MW","room":"3021","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"14:15","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"13:00"},{"days":"R","room":"3021","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"12:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"09:00"}],"start_time":"13:00:00","instructors":["Abigail K. Myers"]}]},
