{"code":"PHYS 160","title":"Astronomy","department":"Physics","credits":1,"description":"A description of the universe, starting with the appearance and organization of the solar system and working outward. Development of the heliocentric view. Observational deduction of properties of stars. Stellar evolution and its relation to pulsars and black holes. Galaxies and the structure and history of the universe.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/phys-physics/100/phys-160","sections":[{"days":"TR","room":"G027","types":["Qlit Course","Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"waitlisted","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":40,"comments":"Open to Seniors, Juniors, Sophomores, & 1st Years","end_time":"11:45:00","meetings":[{"days":"TR","room":"G027","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"11:45","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"10:30"},{"days":"T","room":"G027","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"17:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"14:00"}],"start_time":"10:30:00","instructors":["Katherine A. Brown"]}]},
{"code":"PHYS 190","title":"The Mechanical Universe","department":"Physics","credits":1,"description":"The first semester of a sequence of physics courses for students interested in physical sciences, math or engineering. Normally the first course for students who plan to major or minor in physics. Introduction to principles governing the motion of a particle and of systems of particles. Kinematics and dynamics; energy, linear momentum, angular momentum and conservation laws. Introduction to the laws of special relativity. Sophomores and above need instructor's signature to enroll. Prerequisites, Calculus I (may be taken concurrently). Three hours of class and three hours of laboratory.","cross_listed":[],"catalog_url":"https://hamilton.smartcatalogiq.com/en/current/college-catalogue/courses/phys-physics/100/phys-190","sections":[{"days":"MWF","room":"G041","types":["Qlit Course","Quantitative & Symbolic R"],"status":"open","section":"01","building":"Taylor Science Center","capacity":40,"comments":"Open to First-Years Only. Must sign up for PHYS-190L lab section","end_time":"10:50:00","meetings":[{"days":"MWF","room":"G041","type":"LEC","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-11","end_time":"10:50","start_date":"2026-08-27","start_time":"10:00"},{"days":"W","room":"G041","type":"FINAL","building":"Taylor Science Center","end_date":"2026-12-18","end_time":"22:00","start_date":"2026-12-12","start_time":"19:00"}],"start_time":"10:00:00","instructors":["Adam C. Lark"]}]},
